1) A while back, I wrote a short story (91 lines, to be exact) set in the 
NetHack dungeon.  It's better than that makes it sound (save, perhaps, to
those diehards who think that sounds wonderful).  In fact, it's enough 
better than that that I was wondering about what the copyright bindings on
it are; it features Asidonhopo, a few quotes from the game, and something
reminiscent of a typical nethack situation.  The details of the nethack 
distribution policy, particularly regarding this type of thing, are unknown
to me.  Also, in either case, is this something that anyone would like to
see?

2) Regarding polypiling: just wondering whether anyone actually saw my
suggestion that polymorph wands convert other wands into traps; there seems
to have been no reply to this, which seems odd, given that "leave things 
the way they are" generates 50 rebuttals and responses every time it is 
posted.  This would neatly solve the wishing/polymorph synergy problem, as
well as give the player a way of introducing traps.

